  "body": "Source: review of PR #2503 (merged, 2f965f7d9), comment 6978269279.\n\nWhat happens:\n- `keep_law.rs` lines 105-111: when the corner check cannot run, the code writes only a log line.\n- The band check directly above it adds a note that says the check did not run.\n- The corner check has no such note.\n- Result: material can stay in a corner, and the user sees nothing.\n\nWanted:\n- Add the same \"check did not run\" note for the corner check.\n- Add a test that pins the note.\n\nAlso record:\n- The 0.03 mm noise threshold can hide a real cusp at an obtuse stock corner.\n- At a 150 degree corner with a 10 mm tool, the cusp is about 0.18 mm.\n- The decision file of #2503 accepts this threshold.\n- Review this number against a measured case.\n\nDone means: a corner check that cannot run gives a visible note, and a test pins that note.\n",
